<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:41Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>As glaciers melt, can communities be protected?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:140b5c9b679e4a5cc3a7475df679320ba9dd8b8607cfe9a71873408d05042fbf</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--e5540929272d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b707311b17a3cae23ed3995fa8922aa026b073c50fdfc1ea277e0d5d390f9321</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--5a8297f9dc8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton Peace Agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a91d62cd4c3c9b5ed255b7b433b422099aff5c8e09ba8e2f91b27864617a385f</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--d550ab622814.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh is weighing the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:221464cce13dafb5f3f4cc6064dbbe380fc4e9e898b90e340570da5f1be1a339</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--cfde85175591.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's SPD is fighting for survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8e466ce3f1973c3d564e0212073a72f73442b767ab1255f3048034a098325fa</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448--5e351aab0889.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Social Democratic Party SPD is sinking ever deeper into crisis. Voters are turning away, while unrest is growing within its grassroots ranks. Will the upcoming state elections accelerate the party's downward spiral?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood: Death toll tops 1,000 as rescue continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:653871d3ee6617c4f95e6aed04f316dffe54afbaf0fdc26874c0113277ec83b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460--9fc4d6386c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities say 4,000 people remain unaccounted for as rescue teams with search dogs comb through mud, rocks and debris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:492e143425fea3003e226b18c17f48dad82dd5c6def39f684d0c7375ae5013ef</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--accd083c93a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Explosive devices found near power plant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6c4a161d9af27cd0cae5d9dea00d33992494e7c0ec063e2342e29d761c17eb7</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741--ea7672909059.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police say they found unconventional explosive and incendiary devices near the Jänschwalde power plant in Brandenburg. Meanwhile, Germany's top diplomat says Algeria could become an important supplier of gas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says it will return to ceasefire if US does</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bcb4de8362c0ddb32e6fc40487e0520cac1282c1873594a92deefd6e4a02b91</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-says-it-will-return-to-ceasefire-if-us-does/a-78586314--217c7ae90d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-says-it-will-return-to-ceasefire-if-us-does/a-78586314?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking on the sidelines of the SCO summit in Kyrgyzstan, Iran's president Pezeshkian called on the US to return to the terms of an interim ceasefire deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02bec135a6ce53d6399b2f65c2926d8cf25291ebaf1328cc8513c183ce718727</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate